### Practical 10: Event-Driven Architecture REST Client Tests
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### 1. Server Health Check & EventEmitter Metadata
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Accept: application/json

### 2. View Event Telemetry Stream Initially
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/events/logs
Accept: application/json

### 3. Clear Event Telemetry Stream
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/events/clear
Accept: application/json

### 4. Register New User
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Manan Vasani",
  "email": "event_manan@charusat.edu.in",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 5. Login User & Retrieve Token
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "event_manan@charusat.edu.in",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 6. Set Authentication Token Variable
@authToken = {{login.response.body.token}}

### 7. Create Task: Emits 'task-created' Event Asynchronously
# Note: The HTTP 201 response is returned immediately;
# the console logs notification processing 1500ms later.
# @name createTask
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Evaluate Native EventEmitter Non-Blocking Execution",
  "description": "Practical 10 background email and notification dispatch",
  "priority": "high",
  "completed": false
}

### 8. View Event Telemetry to Confirm 'task-created' Timestamp
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/events/logs
Accept: application/json

### 9. Supplementary 3: Simulate Slow Background Job (e.g. 2500ms delay)
# Demonstrates immediate API response while worker runs in background
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/events/test-slow
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Quarterly Financial PDF Generation",
  "delayMs": 2500
}

### 10. Supplementary 1: Delete Task: Emits 'task-deleted' Event Asynchronously
@taskId = {{createTask.response.body._id}}
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 11. Supplementary 2: Test Error Event Listener Safety
# Emits an error event to verify the listener logs it cleanly without crashing
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/events/test-error
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Simulated push notification gateway timeout"
}

### 12. Inspect Final Event Telemetry & Counters
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/events/logs
Accept: application/json

### 13. Verify Server Remains Live & Responsive
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 14. In-Memory Cache Stats (Practical 9 Baseline)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cache/stats
Accept: application/json
